## 5. Deterministic CLI Plan Verification Gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`)

All automated plan verification gates report strictly **`PASS`** or **`FAIL`** (`NOT_RUN`, `BLOCKED`, and `UNVERIFIED` never count as `PASS`):

| Gate | Command | Pass Criterion |
|---|---|---|
| **G1 — Spec Artifact & AC Presence (`Q1`, `Q2`)** | `{{spec_check_cmd}}` | Approved spec files exist and contain zero unresolved `[UNTESTABLE]` markers (`PASS`) |
| **G2 — Two-Way `AC-NN ↔ TC-NN` Traceability (`Q3`, `Q12`)** | `{{traceability_check_cmd}}` | Every `{{ac_id_format}}` maps to `>= 1` `{{case_id_format}}` and zero orphan cases exist (`PASS`) |
| **G3 — Vague Expectation & Legacy Priority Token Scan (`Q8`, `Q11`)** | `{{plan_lint_cmd}}` | `0` vague expectations (`"works correctly"`) and `0` legacy priority tokens (`PASS`) |

